<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Comparison of topic modeling performance on WikiWeb2M <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burns et al. (2023)</a></cite> and SPIQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pramanick et al. (2024)</a></cite>. We report coherence (NPMI, WE, LLM), diversity (TD), redundancy (I-RBO), and clustering metrics (Purity, ARI, NMI), averaged over <math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\{25,50,75,100\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\{25,50,75,100\}</annotation></semantics></math> with three random seeds. CEMTM consistently outperforms all baselines. See Table <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix D Detailed Results For All Ks ‣ CEMTM: Contextual Embedding-based Multimodal Topic Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Detailed Results For All Ks ‣ CEMTM: Contextual Embedding-based Multimodal Topic Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> for detailed results for each K.</figcaption>
</figure>
